<%- include('../partials/admin_header', {title, flashMsg}) %>
<h1>Backup</h1>
<p class="muted">Every player, blackout date, confirmation, sub, and email log entry lives in one SQLite file. A backup is a point-in-time copy of that file — restoring one puts the whole system back exactly as it was when the backup was taken.</p>

<form method="post" action="/admin/backup" class="card">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Backup now</h2>
  <p class="muted">Safe to run anytime, including while people are actively confirming/subbing — it doesn't pause the app.</p>
  <div class="actions"><button class="btn green" type="submit">Create backup</button></div>
</form>

<div class="notice" style="margin-top:20px;">
  <strong>Set this up once and forget about it:</strong> add a cron job on the Pi so a backup happens automatically every night. From the Pi's terminal: <code>crontab -e</code>, then add a line like
  <pre style="background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--border-width, 1px) var(--border);border-radius:6px;padding:10px;margin:8px 0;overflow-x:auto;font-size:calc(12px * var(--text-scale, 1));">0 2 * * * cd /home/pi/tennis-scheduler && /usr/bin/node src/scripts/backup-db.js >> backup.log 2>&1 && /usr/bin/node src/scripts/backup-offsite.js >> backup.log 2>&1</pre>
  That runs a backup every night at 2am, automatically deletes anything beyond the most recent <%= retention %> (about a month at one a day), then pushes the whole <code>backups/</code> folder to another machine (see below). Full instructions are in README.md under "Backing up the database."
</div>

<% if (offsiteConfigured) { %>
<div class="card" style="margin-top:16px;">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Off-site push</h2>
  <p class="muted">Configured — the cron line above (and the button below) push <code>backups/</code> to the remote machine set in <code>.env</code> via rsync.</p>
  <form method="post" action="/admin/backup/push-offsite" class="inline">
    <button class="btn neutral" type="submit">Push off-site now</button>
  </form>
</div>
<% } else { %>
<div class="flag" style="margin-top:16px;">
  <strong>A backup sitting on the same SD card as the Pi doesn't protect you if the Pi itself dies.</strong> Off-site push isn't configured yet — set <code>OFFSITE_SSH_HOST</code>/<code>OFFSITE_SSH_USER</code>/<code>OFFSITE_SSH_PATH</code> in <code>.env</code> (see README.md's "Get backups off the Pi") to have every backup pushed to another machine automatically. Until then, download a backup below and save it somewhere else yourself every so often.
</div>
<% } %>

<h2>Existing backups</h2>
<% if (backups.length === 0) { %>
  <p class="muted">No backups yet — click "Create backup" above to make the first one.</p>
<% } else { %>
<table class="wide">
  <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Size</th><th>Created</th><th>Actions</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <% backups.forEach(function(b) { %>
      <tr>
        <td><%= b.filename %></td>
        <td><%= (b.size / 1024).toFixed(1) %> KB</td>
        <td><%= b.mtime.toISOString().replace('T', ' ').slice(0, 19) %></td>
        <td>
          <a class="btn small neutral" href="/admin/backup/download/<%= b.filename %>">Download</a>
          <form class="inline" method="post" action="/admin/backup/<%= b.filename %>/delete" onsubmit="return confirm('Delete this backup? This cannot be undone.');">
            <button class="btn small neutral" type="submit">Delete</button>
          </form>
        </td>
      </tr>
    <% }) %>
  </tbody>
</table>
<% } %>

<h2>Restoring from a backup</h2>
<p class="muted">If the database gets corrupted but the Pi itself is fine, restoring is just swapping in the backup file:</p>
<ol class="muted" style="line-height:1.8;">
  <li>Stop the app: <code>pm2 stop tennis-scheduler</code></li>
  <li>Move the backup file onto the Pi as <code>data/tennis.db</code> (overwriting whatever's there) — e.g. <code>cp tennis-backup-20260806-020000123.db data/tennis.db</code> from inside the project folder. Delete <code>data/tennis.db-wal</code> and <code>data/tennis.db-shm</code> if they exist, so nothing stale is left over.</li>
  <li>Restart the app: <code>pm2 start tennis-scheduler</code></li>
  <li>Check <code>/admin</code> loads and the roster/sessions look right.</li>
</ol>
<p class="muted">If the Pi itself is gone, one thing the <code>.db</code> backup does <strong>not</strong> cover: <code>.env</code> (Gmail app password, session secret) lives only on the Pi's disk, never in the database. See "Restoring after the Pi itself is gone" in README.md for the full checklist, including what needs regenerating vs. what you can just make up fresh.</p>
<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
